input.old_string:
// (b) SPLIT selection from accept. The GPU SORT breeds by the coherence-rewarded selFitness (candidate.Fitness),
// so coherent BRIDGES survive as breeding stock. The ACCEPT here uses only the PEEL score (base, carried in the
// Ladder slot as float bits) so the host APPLIES only real progress -- a coherent-but-scrambled bridge breeds
// but is NOT applied (no drift). Uniform across descent/endgame; solved -> peelScore 0 -> always surfaces.
// Sideways (== Score) fires only after a full round-robin pass (Stall); the no-op penalty keeps standing-still
// above Score, so == Score is always a real move to a different equal-peel state.
float candPeel = BitConverter.UInt32BitsToSingle(candidate.Ladder);
bool accept = candPeel < Score || candPeel == Score && Stall >= TGA<TRubikGenome>.StallLimit;

input.new_string:
// Accept: DESCENT compares the (fine) peel Fitness; COHERENT compares the STRUCTURE ladder so structurally-
// equal configs TIE -> sideways fires, which is what escapes a peel LOCAL MINIMUM like the mono-twist (the move
// mono[28] -> 2-block[20] raises the count but lowers the structure, so the ladder accepts it). Fitness < 1
// rejects a Solved-breaker / no-op (Fitness is normalised < 1; >= 1 means a break or a stand-still). GA
// SELECTION is separate: the sort breeds by Fitness, which in COHERENT is the PURE coherence factor.
bool accept = Gpu.Coherent == 0
    ? candidate.Fitness < Score || candidate.Fitness == Score && Stall >= TGA<TRubikGenome>.StallLimit
    : candidate.Fitness < 1f && candidate.Ladder <= ScoreLadder;

